        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "caa6be93-3633-57f7-bd90-4c27eadf684d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ghosts, Battle for Haditha, Tales of the Grim Sleeper\n- People: Nick Broomfield, Lonnie David Franklin Jr.\n- Concepts: Gweilo, Cantonese slang\n- Topics: racial depredation, documentary style\n\nFacts:\n- Ghosts is a 2006 film whose title references the Cantonese slang term \"Gweilo\" (鬼佬), meaning \"ghost man,\" which is used for white people.\n- In its unmodified form, Gweilo applies only to people of European ethnicities and has a history of racially deprecatory use.\n- Battle for Haditha dramatizes real events using a documentary style and is Nick Broomfield's follow-up to Ghosts.\n- Tales of the Grim Sleeper is a 2014 feature-length documentary film by Nick Broomfield about the serial killer Lonnie David Franklin Jr., who was nicknamed the Grim Sleeper.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "44d5e541-15c9-5c9d-8058-0fafb75078af",
        "text": "Page: Ghosts (2006 film). Sentence: The title is a reference to the Cantonese slang term \"Gweilo\" (鬼佬), meaning \"ghost man\", used for white people.\nPage: Gweilo. Sentence: In its unmodified form, it applies only to European ethnicities and has a history of racially deprecatory use.\nPage: Battle for Haditha. Sentence: Dramatising real events using a documentary style, \"Battle for Haditha\" is Broomfield's follow up to \"Ghosts.\"\nPage: Tales of the Grim Sleeper. Sentence: Tales of the Grim Sleeper is a 2014 feature-length documentary film by Nick Broomfield about the serial killer Lonnie David Franklin Jr., nicknamed the Grim Sleeper.",
